contentText:
Hip-hop was founded in the Bronx in 1973, and 53 years later, New York City&#8217;s Mayor Zohran Mamdani wants to restore the Big Apple to rap capital glory and remain the genre&#8217;s centrifugal force.

In a new short documentary that Billboard exclusively premieres on Wednesday (Sept. 30), Mamdani sits down with Nas to discuss the state of hip-hop in New York City, its origins and the future.

