&#8220;We can’t be content with New York City simply being the birthplace of hip-hop,&#8221; Mamdani tells Billboard . &#8220;We want it to still be its home, and that means ensuring that the artists who create here are actually able to live here.&#8221;&nbsp;

The mayor is also working to continue solving the city&#8217;s housing crisis: &#8220;If we allow New York to become such an expensive city that art becomes a luxury good, then we are depriving future generations from the magic of art. New Yorkers deserve a city that is a living, breathing testament to what it looks like when we create the conditions to help this art form flourish.&#8221;

Mamdani, who once rapped under the alias Mr. Cardamom, spoke with Nas at a park nearby, where the rap deity was raised in the Queensbridge Projects.

“Hip-hop unveils the truth. Hip-hop tells you exactly what your city looks like, sounds like, feels like,&#8221; Nas says in the doc while rocking a vintage New York Mets Darryl Strawberry jersey. &#8220;It was an outcry from people who demanded things to change and to tell the world what we were going through. And that came from a city that was going through a whole lot.&#8221;

The clip also recaps the mayor&#8217;s trip to the Bronx School of Hip-Hop on the first day of classes earlier in September. Located in the Claremont section of the borough, hip-hop serves as the foundation of the school&#8217;s curriculum. Students opened up about their journey and hip-hop&#8217;s influence, while Fat Joe made a cameo.

&#8220;It&#8217;s, like, surreal that New York City Mayor&#8217;s Office, the chancellor&#8217;s office &#8212; this is their school. They said we are going to back this,&#8221; adds School of Hip-Hop principal Jason Reyes. &#8220;Who would have ever thought that hip-hop would make it this far? So, it means the world to know that our city is leading the way in a way that no one else has ever done it. And that&#8217;s New York.&#8221;

At just 34 years old, Mamdani became the city’s first Muslim and South Asian mayor in 2025. His policies have even drawn the ire of one of his favorite rappers , 50 Cent, but the mayor still has plenty of love for the G-Unit leader.

